Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:35:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 079/154] feat(startup): the window opens finished, not in
 three arrivals
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The window used to show on the system fill, then the sidebar page
loaded empty, then the rows drew, then the tint landed, none of them
waiting for the other.

THE SPACE TINT is painted at window construction, so the first frame is
the window's own colour.

THE SIDEBAR stays at opacity 0 until its first render marks the root
drawn, then fades in over 200ms as one piece.

THE FIRST SHOW waits for that render or a 700ms cap, whichever comes
first, and logs which. StartupHold owns the wait and fires once.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

